# Nissan Note E12 five-door hatchback, 2013-2016.
#
# The second-generation Note, built on a Renault platform and a quite different
# car from the E11: lower, more sculpted, with a rising waistline and a tapered
# front quarter glass.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Note
#
# Dimensions 4.100 x 1.695 x 1.535 m, wheelbase 2.600 m, from the English
# Wikipedia E12 dimension box. Mirrors take the modelled width to 1.902 m.
#
# Colours. No UK colour chart for the E12 was located, so the objects carry plain
# colour names: white, red, silver and blue. Weights white 3, red 3, silver 2,
# blue 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 170 km/h for the 1.2 DIG-S, the volume model. Comfort 85/458, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 85, the same as the E11 despite the lower body. Classes 0,1.
#
# Dates are road presence: September 2013 intro, retires staggered 2028-2031 on a
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-note-e12.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-note-e12.dae (43 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-note-e12/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Recorded limitations: no strict side profile exists, so the proportions are
# dimension-calibrated. The builder flagged the body corners and bumpers as too
# square, the headlamp surfaces as needing correction and the rear lamps as
# irregular. Those were judged not to read at 128 px, so the model was installed
# rather than spending a correction round; at pak scale the rising waist, the
# tapered quarter glass and the tall hatch outline carry the identity.

